WEBVTT

00:00:03.651 --> 00:00:04.919
Dad. Sam.

00:00:04.954 --> 00:00:06.557
This is bigger than you
think. They're everywhere.

00:00:06.591 --> 00:00:08.528
Sam: if this demon killed mom
and jess and dad's closing in,

00:00:08.561 --> 00:00:09.730
We got to help.

00:00:09.764 --> 00:00:11.299
Dad doesn't want our help.

00:00:11.333 --> 00:00:14.673
I'm talking one week here, man,
to get answers, to get revenge.

00:00:14.707 --> 00:00:15.941
You think i didn't respect dad.

00:00:15.976 --> 00:00:17.613
Sorry i brought it up. I respected him.

00:00:17.646 --> 00:00:19.617
No matter what i did,
it was never good enough.

00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:21.319
So what are you saying? That
dad was disappointed in you?

00:00:21.353 --> 00:00:22.990
When we finally do find dad,

00:00:23.023 --> 00:00:25.829
I don't know if he's
even gonna want to see me.

00:00:25.862 --> 00:00:27.666
Hey! Dad.

00:00:27.699 --> 00:00:28.835
Hey, boys.

00:00:28.868 --> 00:00:31.039
Hi, sam. Hi, dad.

00:00:31.072 --> 00:00:33.678
Last time we were together,
we had one hell of a fight.

00:00:33.711 --> 00:00:36.183
Yes, sir. It's good to see you again.

00:00:36.216 --> 00:00:38.120
It's been a long time.

00:00:38.153 --> 00:00:39.155
Sam!

00:00:39.189 --> 00:00:40.491
Dean: we almost got dad killed.

00:00:40.525 --> 00:00:42.061
They're not gonna stop.
They're gonna try again.

00:00:42.094 --> 00:00:43.798
They're gonna use us to get to him.

00:00:43.832 --> 00:00:45.569
Dad's vulnerable when he's with us.

00:00:45.602 --> 00:00:47.071
I got to be a part of this fight.

00:00:47.104 --> 00:00:48.708
Sammy, this fight is just starting.

00:00:48.741 --> 00:00:50.812
You got to let me go.

00:01:11.186 --> 00:01:12.723
Beth: mr. Elkins?

00:01:15.294 --> 00:01:16.463
Mr. Elkins.

00:01:16.496 --> 00:01:18.567
Would you like another?

00:01:18.601 --> 00:01:21.239
Yeah. Thanks, beth.

00:01:24.178 --> 00:01:26.516
I thought they caught the unabomber.

00:01:26.550 --> 00:01:29.757
Yeah, poor mr. Elkins lives
all alone up in the canyon.

00:01:29.790 --> 00:01:32.528
Same seat every day,

00:01:32.562 --> 00:01:34.833
Going through his papers,
making his little notes.

00:01:34.867 --> 00:01:38.140
He's a nice old man. He's just a nut.

00:01:40.812 --> 00:01:42.348
Here you go.

00:02:08.033 --> 00:02:09.302
What'll you have?

00:02:09.335 --> 00:02:11.774
Jack all around. Leave the bottle.

00:02:11.807 --> 00:02:14.445
You hungry? We have dinner plans.

00:02:18.654 --> 00:02:21.126
Can i get you something
else, mr. Elkins?

00:03:08.921 --> 00:03:11.059
It's been a while.

00:03:11.092 --> 00:03:13.163
I got to say, you look old.

00:03:13.196 --> 00:03:15.501
What do you want? What do you think?

00:03:17.671 --> 00:03:19.008
Damn.

00:03:23.550 --> 00:03:24.819
You can do better than that.

00:03:36.109 --> 00:03:37.645
Come on, come on.

00:04:19.963 --> 00:04:21.299
Nice gun.

00:04:23.402 --> 00:04:26.075
Wouldn't do you much good, of course.

00:04:26.109 --> 00:04:28.613
Boys...

00:04:28.647 --> 00:04:31.052
We're eating in tonight.

00:04:51.359 --> 00:04:53.930
All right, dude, not a decent
lead in all of nebraska.

00:04:53.964 --> 00:04:55.167
What do you got?

00:04:55.200 --> 00:04:58.139
Well, i been scanning wyoming,
colorado, south dakota.

00:04:58.173 --> 00:05:01.279
Here
- A woman in iowa fell 10,000 feet from an airplane

00:05:01.312 --> 00:05:03.049
And survived.

00:05:03.083 --> 00:05:04.852
Sounds more like "that's incredible!"

00:05:04.885 --> 00:05:06.456
Than "the twilight zone."

00:05:06.488 --> 00:05:07.691
Yeah.

00:05:07.725 --> 00:05:10.630
Hey, you know, we could
just keep heading east -

00:05:10.664 --> 00:05:12.868
New york, upstate.

00:05:12.901 --> 00:05:15.240
Could stop by and see sarah again. Huh?

00:05:15.273 --> 00:05:17.845
She's a cool chick, man. Smokin'.

00:05:17.878 --> 00:05:21.386
You two seemed pretty
friendly. What do you say?

00:05:21.419 --> 00:05:23.390
Yeah, i don't know. Maybe someday.

00:05:23.423 --> 00:05:26.162
But in the meantime, we got
a lot of work to do, dean,

00:05:26.195 --> 00:05:27.398
And you know that.

00:05:27.431 --> 00:05:29.101
Yeah, you're right.

00:05:29.135 --> 00:05:31.339
What else you got?

00:05:31.372 --> 00:05:32.608
Uh, man in colorado.

00:05:32.641 --> 00:05:34.979
Local man by the name of daniel elkins

00:05:35.012 --> 00:05:36.883
Was found mauled in his home.

00:05:36.916 --> 00:05:39.455
Elkins. I know that name.

00:05:39.488 --> 00:05:41.459
Doesn't ring a bell.

00:05:41.492 --> 00:05:43.496
Looks like the cops
don't know what to think.

00:05:43.530 --> 00:05:46.869
At first they said it was
some sort of bear attack,

00:05:46.903 --> 00:05:49.208
And now they found signs of robbery.

00:05:49.241 --> 00:05:50.609
Mm-Hmm.

00:05:50.644 --> 00:05:52.815
Yeah.

00:05:56.322 --> 00:05:58.293
Here. Check it out.

00:06:04.137 --> 00:06:05.974
You think it's the same elkins?

00:06:06.007 --> 00:06:08.313
It's a colorado area code.

00:06:46.422 --> 00:06:48.993
Looks like the maid didn't come today.

00:06:54.772 --> 00:06:57.243
Hey, there's salt over
here, right inside the door.

00:06:57.277 --> 00:06:59.515
You mean, like,
protection-Against-Demon salt

00:06:59.548 --> 00:07:01.485
Or "oops, i spilled the popcorn" salt?

00:07:01.519 --> 00:07:03.222
It's clearly a ring.

00:07:07.698 --> 00:07:10.904
You think this guy elkins was a player?

00:07:10.937 --> 00:07:12.006
Definitely.

00:07:21.492 --> 00:07:23.963
That looks a hell of a lot like dad's.

00:07:23.997 --> 00:07:27.437
Except this dates back to the '60s.

00:07:52.421 --> 00:07:55.560
Whatever attacked him, looks
like there was more than one.

00:07:55.593 --> 00:07:58.198
Looks like he put up
a hell of a fight, too.

00:07:58.231 --> 00:08:00.603
Yeah.

00:08:27.056 --> 00:08:29.293
Got something?

00:08:30.964 --> 00:08:33.970
I don't know. Some
scratches in the floor.

00:08:34.003 --> 00:08:35.305
Death throes maybe?

00:08:35.339 --> 00:08:37.176
Maybe.

00:08:56.381 --> 00:08:58.118
Or maybe a message.

00:09:00.890 --> 00:09:04.263
Look familiar?

00:09:04.297 --> 00:09:06.535
Three letters, six digits -

00:09:06.569 --> 00:09:10.577
The location and combination
of a post office box.

00:09:10.610 --> 00:09:11.912
It's a mail drop.

00:09:11.946 --> 00:09:13.883
That's just the way dad does it.

00:09:32.721 --> 00:09:36.862
"J.W."
- You think? John winchester?

00:09:36.896 --> 00:09:38.900
I don't know. Should we open it?

00:09:43.073 --> 00:09:44.912
Dad?

00:09:47.483 --> 00:09:49.788
Dad, what are you doing
here? Are you all right?

00:09:49.821 --> 00:09:50.857
Yeah, i'm okay.

00:09:50.890 --> 00:09:52.393
Look, i read the news about daniel.

00:09:52.426 --> 00:09:55.032
I got here as fast as i could.

00:09:56.802 --> 00:09:59.240
I saw you two up at his place.

00:09:59.273 --> 00:10:01.044
Why didn't you come in, dad?

00:10:01.076 --> 00:10:02.346
You know why.

00:10:02.379 --> 00:10:05.084
Because i had to make sure
you weren't followed...

00:10:05.117 --> 00:10:06.889
By anyone...

00:10:06.922 --> 00:10:08.592
Or anything.

00:10:08.625 --> 00:10:11.966
Nice job of covering
your tracks, by the way.

00:10:11.999 --> 00:10:14.871
Yeah, well, we learned from the best.

00:10:14.905 --> 00:10:17.877
Wait, so you came all the way
out here for this elkins guy?

00:10:17.911 --> 00:10:19.080
Yeah.

00:10:19.112 --> 00:10:22.988
He was
- He was a good man.

00:10:23.021 --> 00:10:25.459
He taught me a hell
of a lot about hunting.

00:10:25.492 --> 00:10:28.966
You never mentioned him to us.

00:10:29.000 --> 00:10:31.537
We had a -

00:10:31.571 --> 00:10:34.210
We had kind of a falling out.

00:10:34.243 --> 00:10:36.882
I hadn't seen him in years.

00:10:38.753 --> 00:10:40.957
I should look at that.

00:10:49.507 --> 00:10:53.581
"If you're reading
this, i'm already dead."

00:10:53.615 --> 00:10:55.887
That son of a bitch. What is it?

00:10:55.920 --> 00:10:58.223
He had it the whole time. Dad, what?

00:10:58.258 --> 00:10:59.761
When you searched the place,

00:10:59.795 --> 00:11:02.198
Did you see a gun, an
antique, a colt revolver?

00:11:02.231 --> 00:11:03.334
Did you see it?

00:11:03.368 --> 00:11:05.572
Uh, there was an old
case, but it was empty.

00:11:05.605 --> 00:11:07.509
They have it. You mean
whatever killed elkins?

00:11:07.543 --> 00:11:09.413
We got to pick up their trail.

00:11:10.950 --> 00:11:13.923
Wait. You want us to come with you?

00:11:13.956 --> 00:11:16.294
If elkins is telling the truth,
we've got to find this gun.

00:11:16.327 --> 00:11:18.799
The gun? Why? Because
it's important, that's why.

00:11:18.833 --> 00:11:21.104
Dad, we don't even know
what these things are yet.

00:11:21.137 --> 00:11:23.141
They were what danny
elkins killed best...

00:11:23.174 --> 00:11:25.312
Vampires.

00:11:25.345 --> 00:11:26.347
Vampires?

00:11:26.380 --> 00:11:28.250
I thought there was no such thing.

00:11:28.283 --> 00:11:30.522
You never even mentioned them, dad.

00:11:30.555 --> 00:11:32.927
I thought they were extinct.

00:11:32.961 --> 00:11:37.002
I thought elkins and
others had wiped them out.

00:11:40.375 --> 00:11:41.744
I was wrong.

00:11:43.748 --> 00:11:47.122
John: most vampire lore is
crap. A cross won't repel them.

00:11:47.156 --> 00:11:48.591
Sunlight won't kill them

00:11:48.625 --> 00:11:50.963
And neither will a stake to the heart.

00:11:50.997 --> 00:11:53.234
But the bloodlust
- That part's true.

00:11:53.268 --> 00:11:55.572
They need fresh human blood to survive.

00:11:55.605 --> 00:11:57.009
They were once people,

00:11:57.042 --> 00:12:00.282
So you won't know it's a
vampire until it's too late.

00:12:00.314 --> 00:12:02.052
All yours, baby.

00:12:08.398 --> 00:12:10.535
What?

00:12:10.569 --> 00:12:12.338
Well, i guess you showed that guy.

00:12:12.371 --> 00:12:15.145
What guy? The guy who bet you
you wouldn't buy that shirt.

00:12:15.178 --> 00:12:17.381
I love this shirt.

00:12:20.055 --> 00:12:21.490
Look out!

00:12:25.866 --> 00:12:27.569
What happened to him?

00:12:27.603 --> 00:12:29.372
Call 911.

00:12:53.184 --> 00:12:55.755
Man: 22, i'm going out there.

00:12:55.789 --> 00:12:57.593
Man #2: copy that.

00:13:03.071 --> 00:13:06.409
Sam, dean, let's go.

00:13:06.443 --> 00:13:07.746
Picked up a police call.

00:13:07.779 --> 00:13:08.948
What happened?

00:13:08.982 --> 00:13:11.453
A couple called 911. They
found a body in the street.

00:13:11.486 --> 00:13:13.291
Cops got there. Everyone was missing.

00:13:13.324 --> 00:13:14.526
It's the vampires.

00:13:14.560 --> 00:13:15.962
How do you know?

00:13:15.996 --> 00:13:17.833
Just follow me, okay?

00:13:20.238 --> 00:13:21.974
Vampires.

00:13:22.008 --> 00:13:24.313
It's funny every time i hear it.

00:13:24.346 --> 00:13:26.516
[ Indistinct chatter on police radio ]

00:13:30.491 --> 00:13:32.896
I don't see why we couldn't
have gone over with him.

00:13:32.930 --> 00:13:34.867
Oh, don't tell me it's already starting.

00:13:34.900 --> 00:13:37.004
What's starting?

00:13:37.038 --> 00:13:38.775
What do you got? It was them all right.

00:13:38.808 --> 00:13:40.412
It looks like they're heading west.

00:13:40.444 --> 00:13:42.548
We have to double back
to get around that detour.

00:13:42.582 --> 00:13:43.952
How can you be so sure?

00:13:43.985 --> 00:13:45.922
I just want to know we're
going in the right direction.

00:13:45.956 --> 00:13:47.592
We are.

00:13:47.626 --> 00:13:49.529
How do you know?

00:13:49.562 --> 00:13:51.600
I found this.

00:13:53.771 --> 00:13:56.911
What is it? A vampire fang?

00:13:56.944 --> 00:14:00.084
No fangs
- Teeth. The second set descends when they attack.

00:14:00.118 --> 00:14:01.787
Any more questions?

00:14:05.027 --> 00:14:07.299
Let's get out of here.
We're losing daylight.

00:14:07.332 --> 00:14:11.106
And, dean, why don't you touch
up your car before you get rust?

00:14:11.140 --> 00:14:13.010
I wouldn't have given you the damn thing

00:14:13.043 --> 00:14:15.648
If i thought you were gonna ruin it.

00:14:22.896 --> 00:14:24.900
Vampires nest in groups of 8 to 10.

00:14:24.933 --> 00:14:27.339
Smaller packs are sent
out to hunt for food.

00:14:27.372 --> 00:14:30.611
Victims are taken to the nest,
where the pack keeps them alive,

00:14:30.644 --> 00:14:32.516
Bleeding them for days or weeks.

00:14:32.548 --> 00:14:35.221
I wonder if that's what
happened to that 911 couple.

00:14:35.255 --> 00:14:37.225
That's probably what dad's thinking.

00:14:37.259 --> 00:14:41.867
Of course, it would be nice if
he just told us what he thinks.

00:14:41.901 --> 00:14:43.738
<i>So it is starting.</i>

00:14:43.771 --> 00:14:46.477
What?

00:14:46.510 --> 00:14:48.381
Sam, we've been looking
for dad all year.

00:14:48.414 --> 00:14:50.752
Now we're not with him for
more than a couple of hours

00:14:50.785 --> 00:14:51.954
And there's static already.

00:14:51.987 --> 00:14:54.726
No.

00:14:54.760 --> 00:14:56.997
Look, i'm happy he's okay, all right,

00:14:57.031 --> 00:14:58.901
And i'm happy that we're
all working together.

00:14:58.935 --> 00:15:00.805
Good.

00:15:00.839 --> 00:15:05.013
It's just the way he treats
us like we're children.

00:15:05.047 --> 00:15:06.484
He barks orders at us, dean.

00:15:06.517 --> 00:15:08.855
He expects us to follow
him without question.

00:15:08.888 --> 00:15:11.192
He keeps us on some
crap need-To-Know deal.

00:15:11.226 --> 00:15:13.163
He does what he does for
a reason. What reason?

00:15:13.196 --> 00:15:14.399
Our job!

00:15:14.433 --> 00:15:16.236
There's no time to argue.
There's no margin for error.

00:15:16.270 --> 00:15:17.738
It's just the way the
old man runs things.

00:15:17.772 --> 00:15:19.642
Yeah, well, maybe that
worked when we were kids,

00:15:19.675 --> 00:15:21.012
But not anymore, all right?

00:15:21.045 --> 00:15:23.250
Not after everything you and
i have been through, dean.

00:15:23.284 --> 00:15:25.721
Are you telling me you're cool
with just falling into line

00:15:25.754 --> 00:15:27.392
And letting him run the whole show?

00:15:28.961 --> 00:15:32.636
If that's what it takes.

00:15:56.816 --> 00:15:58.921
Have some beer, buddy.

00:15:58.955 --> 00:16:01.159
It'll calm your nerves.

00:16:01.192 --> 00:16:02.629
No, thanks.

00:16:02.662 --> 00:16:03.931
Oh, come on.

00:16:03.965 --> 00:16:06.403
You drink enough, i can
taste it in your blood.

00:16:06.437 --> 00:16:08.139
That's gross.

00:16:15.955 --> 00:16:17.659
Well, how about you, babe?

00:16:25.942 --> 00:16:27.177
Attagirl.

00:16:33.823 --> 00:16:36.062
Bo! Wait for luther.

00:16:58.206 --> 00:17:00.944
I missed you, too, baby.

00:17:00.978 --> 00:17:03.584
We've got presents.

00:17:10.030 --> 00:17:11.466
She looks interesting.

00:17:13.537 --> 00:17:14.539
Hmm.

00:17:17.177 --> 00:17:18.413
He doesn't.

00:17:18.446 --> 00:17:19.783
Lock him up.

00:17:22.655 --> 00:17:25.695
On second thought, go
ahead and treat yourself.

00:17:30.772 --> 00:17:34.278
[ Crying ] no!

00:17:34.311 --> 00:17:35.848
There's something else.

00:17:37.819 --> 00:17:39.255
This all theirs?

00:17:39.288 --> 00:17:42.662
No. It's from an old friend of yours...

00:17:42.695 --> 00:17:44.198
Daniel elkins.

00:17:44.231 --> 00:17:46.169
I caught his scent.

00:17:46.202 --> 00:17:48.707
I thought i'd surprise you.

00:17:48.741 --> 00:17:50.611
Kate, what did you do?

00:17:50.645 --> 00:17:52.347
I made him suffer.

00:17:52.381 --> 00:17:54.452
You shouldn't have done that.

00:17:54.485 --> 00:17:55.855
There are others like him.

00:17:55.888 --> 00:17:57.892
They'll know the signs
and come looking for us.

00:17:57.926 --> 00:17:58.993
We have to be careful.

00:17:59.027 --> 00:18:00.297
Luther, i did it for you,

00:18:00.330 --> 00:18:01.834
For what he did to your family.

00:18:01.867 --> 00:18:03.871
Revenge isn't worth
much if you end up dead.

00:18:07.076 --> 00:18:08.747
I'm sorry, babe.

00:18:08.781 --> 00:18:11.118
I'm sorry.

00:18:17.029 --> 00:18:19.033
I thought you might like that.

00:18:19.067 --> 00:18:21.807
Looks like it was made
around the time you were born.

00:18:23.844 --> 00:18:25.715
I've seen this before.

00:18:25.748 --> 00:18:28.286
Elkins died with it in his hands.

00:18:28.319 --> 00:18:32.227
He should have known better
- Using a gun.

00:18:32.261 --> 00:18:35.634
This is no ordinary gun.

00:18:35.668 --> 00:18:37.805
Yeah, dad. All right, got it.

00:18:37.839 --> 00:18:39.910
Pull off the next exit. Why?

00:18:39.943 --> 00:18:41.980
'Cause dad thinks we
got the vampires' trail.

00:18:42.014 --> 00:18:43.048
How?

00:18:43.081 --> 00:18:45.287
I don't know. He didn't say.

00:18:56.810 --> 00:18:59.381
Oh, crap. Here we go.

00:18:59.415 --> 00:19:01.252
What the hell was that? We need to talk.

00:19:01.285 --> 00:19:02.722
About what? About everything.

00:19:02.755 --> 00:19:05.260
Where we going, dad? What's
the big deal about this gun?

00:19:05.293 --> 00:19:07.364
We can q&a after we
kill all the vampires.

00:19:07.397 --> 00:19:09.635
Your brother's right. We
don't have time for this.

00:19:09.668 --> 00:19:12.040
Last we saw you, you said it
was too dangerous to be together.

00:19:12.074 --> 00:19:13.676
Now, out of the blue, you need our help.

00:19:13.710 --> 00:19:16.114
Obviously something big's going
down, and we want to know what!

00:19:16.147 --> 00:19:18.252
Get back in the car. No.

00:19:18.286 --> 00:19:20.523
I said get back in the damn car.

00:19:20.557 --> 00:19:21.927
Yeah, and i said no.

00:19:21.960 --> 00:19:23.630
All right, you made
your point, tough guy.

00:19:23.663 --> 00:19:25.901
Look, we're all tired. We
can talk about this later.

00:19:25.935 --> 00:19:27.203
Sammy, i mean it. Come on.

00:19:27.236 --> 00:19:28.874
This is why i left in the first place.

00:19:28.907 --> 00:19:30.778
What'd you say? You heard me.

00:19:30.811 --> 00:19:31.847
<i>Yeah, you left.</i>

00:19:31.880 --> 00:19:34.318
Your brother and me
- We needed you.

00:19:34.351 --> 00:19:36.890
You walked away, sam. You walked away!

00:19:36.923 --> 00:19:39.361
You're the one who said,
"don't come back," dad.

00:19:39.395 --> 00:19:41.666
You're the one who
closed that door, not me!

00:19:41.699 --> 00:19:44.471
You were just pissed off you
couldn't control me anymore!

00:19:44.505 --> 00:19:46.207
Stop it! Stop it! Stop it!

00:19:46.241 --> 00:19:48.245
That's enough!

00:19:49.748 --> 00:19:51.352
That means you, too.

00:19:59.200 --> 00:20:00.770
Terrific.

00:20:24.084 --> 00:20:26.155
Luther: you like to watch, huh?

00:20:26.188 --> 00:20:28.358
Me too.

00:20:30.630 --> 00:20:32.299
Ready, baby?

00:20:46.695 --> 00:20:49.902
Are you gonna kill me?

00:20:49.936 --> 00:20:54.377
I'm gonna take you so high
you're never gonna come down.

00:21:32.386 --> 00:21:34.758
Welcome home, baby.

00:21:52.133 --> 00:21:53.736
I know what time it is.

00:21:53.769 --> 00:21:55.239
Get in.

00:21:58.580 --> 00:22:01.653
Dean: son of a bitch.

00:22:01.685 --> 00:22:04.157
So they're really not afraid of the sun?

00:22:04.191 --> 00:22:07.029
No, direct sunlight hurts
like a nasty sunburn.

00:22:07.062 --> 00:22:10.937
The only way to kill
them is by beheading.

00:22:10.970 --> 00:22:14.411
And, yeah, they sleep during the day.

00:22:14.444 --> 00:22:17.850
It doesn't mean they won't wake up.

00:22:17.884 --> 00:22:21.358
So i guess walking right
in's not our best option.

00:22:21.391 --> 00:22:24.264
Actually, that's the plan.

00:22:32.313 --> 00:22:33.916
Dad, i've got an extra
machete if you need one.

00:22:33.949 --> 00:22:37.457
Think i'm okay. Thanks.

00:22:37.490 --> 00:22:39.427
Wow.

00:22:46.107 --> 00:22:48.879
So...

00:22:48.912 --> 00:22:51.585
You boys really want
to know about this colt?

00:22:55.694 --> 00:22:57.230
Yes, sir.

00:22:57.263 --> 00:22:59.702
It's just a story...

00:22:59.735 --> 00:23:02.708
A legend, really.

00:23:02.741 --> 00:23:04.844
Well, i thought it was.

00:23:04.878 --> 00:23:07.850
Never really believed it
until i read daniel's letter.

00:23:07.884 --> 00:23:11.759
Back in 1835, when
halley's comet was overhead,

00:23:11.793 --> 00:23:15.399
The same night those
men died at the alamo,

00:23:15.433 --> 00:23:18.339
They say samuel colt made a gun...

00:23:18.372 --> 00:23:19.641
A special gun.

00:23:19.674 --> 00:23:21.746
He made it for a hunter -

00:23:21.779 --> 00:23:25.151
A man like us, only on horseback.

00:23:25.185 --> 00:23:28.124
The story goes he made 13 bullets.

00:23:28.157 --> 00:23:32.099
This hunter used the
gun a half dozen times

00:23:32.132 --> 00:23:36.441
Before he disappeared,
the gun along with him.

00:23:36.475 --> 00:23:39.948
Somehow, daniel got his hands on it.

00:23:39.981 --> 00:23:42.286
They say -

00:23:42.320 --> 00:23:44.958
They say this gun can kill anything.

00:23:44.991 --> 00:23:48.432
Kill anything, like
supernatural anything?

00:23:49.667 --> 00:23:51.438
Like the demon.

00:23:51.471 --> 00:23:53.308
Yeah, the demon.

00:23:53.342 --> 00:23:56.213
Ever since i picked up its trail,

00:23:56.247 --> 00:24:00.423
I've been looking for a
way to destroy that thing.

00:24:00.456 --> 00:24:04.364
Find the gun...

00:24:04.397 --> 00:24:06.903
We may have it.

00:25:38.752 --> 00:25:40.689
Sam: dean.

00:26:04.671 --> 00:26:06.473
There's more.

00:26:41.510 --> 00:26:44.049
Hey.

00:26:44.082 --> 00:26:46.154
Hey, hey, shh. I'm here to help you.

00:26:58.745 --> 00:27:00.414
John: boys, run!

00:27:01.316 --> 00:27:02.519
Dad!

00:27:10.803 --> 00:27:12.372
Dad?!

00:27:14.710 --> 00:27:16.446
Dad?!

00:27:21.690 --> 00:27:23.995
They won't follow. They'll till tonight.

00:27:24.029 --> 00:27:26.433
Once a vampire gets your
scent, it's for life.

00:27:26.466 --> 00:27:27.669
What do we do now?

00:27:27.702 --> 00:27:29.774
You got to find the
nearest funeral home.

00:27:32.545 --> 00:27:34.951
It shouldn't be taking this long.

00:27:34.984 --> 00:27:37.422
I should go help.

00:27:37.455 --> 00:27:39.827
Dean's got it.

00:27:47.375 --> 00:27:49.212
Sammy.

00:27:50.883 --> 00:27:51.885
Yeah?

00:27:54.824 --> 00:27:57.363
I don't think i ever told you this,

00:27:57.395 --> 00:28:00.635
But the day you were
born, you know what i did?

00:28:00.668 --> 00:28:02.739
No.

00:28:02.772 --> 00:28:05.846
I put 100 bucks into a
savings account for you.

00:28:05.879 --> 00:28:08.484
I did the same thing for your brother.

00:28:11.256 --> 00:28:12.792
It was a college fund.

00:28:15.131 --> 00:28:20.308
And every month, i'd put
in another $100 until...

00:28:22.346 --> 00:28:24.749
Anyway, my point is, sam, that

00:28:26.753 --> 00:28:28.892
This is never the life
that i wanted for you.

00:28:28.925 --> 00:28:31.630
Then why'd you get so mad when i left?

00:28:31.663 --> 00:28:35.171
You got to understand something.

00:28:35.204 --> 00:28:37.775
After your mother passed,

00:28:37.809 --> 00:28:41.650
All i saw was evil, everywhere.

00:28:41.683 --> 00:28:47.228
And all i cared about was
keeping you boys alive.

00:28:47.261 --> 00:28:50.735
I wanted you prepared...

00:28:50.768 --> 00:28:52.271
Ready.

00:28:54.509 --> 00:28:57.115
So somewhere along the line, i, uh

00:28:59.819 --> 00:29:01.823
I stopped being your father.

00:29:01.857 --> 00:29:03.727
And i -

00:29:03.761 --> 00:29:07.436
I became your drill sergeant.

00:29:09.473 --> 00:29:13.280
So when you said you
wanted to go away to school,

00:29:13.313 --> 00:29:16.586
All i could think
about, my only thought,

00:29:16.620 --> 00:29:21.663
Was that you were gonna be alone...

00:29:21.696 --> 00:29:23.634
Vulnerable.

00:29:23.667 --> 00:29:26.474
Sammy, it just -

00:29:26.507 --> 00:29:28.644
It never occurred to me what you wanted.

00:29:30.515 --> 00:29:32.819
I just couldn't accept the fact

00:29:32.852 --> 00:29:35.624
That you and me...

00:29:35.658 --> 00:29:36.827
We're just different.

00:29:38.430 --> 00:29:39.699
What?

00:29:42.972 --> 00:29:44.543
We're not different.

00:29:46.980 --> 00:29:49.119
Not anymore.

00:29:51.923 --> 00:29:54.629
With what happened to mom and jess

00:29:58.403 --> 00:30:00.474
We probably have a lot more in common

00:30:00.508 --> 00:30:03.213
Than just about anyone.

00:30:05.585 --> 00:30:07.955
I guess you're right, son.

00:30:11.696 --> 00:30:13.867
Hey, dad?

00:30:16.072 --> 00:30:18.076
Whatever happened to that college fund?

00:30:20.046 --> 00:30:21.850
Spent it on ammo.

00:30:28.931 --> 00:30:30.301
Whoo!

00:30:30.334 --> 00:30:33.840
Man, there's some heavy security
to protect a bunch of dead guys.

00:30:33.874 --> 00:30:36.045
Did you get it?

00:30:45.531 --> 00:30:48.437
You know what to do.

00:30:57.355 --> 00:30:59.024
Kate: car trouble?

00:31:03.200 --> 00:31:05.404
Let me give you a lift...

00:31:05.437 --> 00:31:07.341
Take you back to my place.

00:31:07.375 --> 00:31:08.477
I'll pass.

00:31:08.510 --> 00:31:10.848
I usually draw the line at necrophilia.

00:31:25.176 --> 00:31:28.817
I don't normally get this
friendly till the second date.

00:31:28.850 --> 00:31:31.890
You know, we could have some fun.

00:31:31.923 --> 00:31:35.096
I always like to make new friends.

00:31:45.016 --> 00:31:47.888
Oh, sorry.

00:31:47.922 --> 00:31:50.327
I never really stay
with a chick that long.

00:31:50.361 --> 00:31:51.663
Definitely not eternity.

00:31:51.696 --> 00:31:52.932
Ugh!

00:31:57.375 --> 00:31:59.379
Damn it.

00:32:00.881 --> 00:32:02.718
Barely even stings.

00:32:02.752 --> 00:32:05.089
Give it time, sweetheart.

00:32:05.123 --> 00:32:07.361
That arrow's soaked in dead man's blood.

00:32:07.395 --> 00:32:09.833
It's like poison to you, isn't it?

00:32:13.105 --> 00:32:14.409
Load her up.

00:32:14.442 --> 00:32:16.847
I'll take care of this one.

00:32:27.525 --> 00:32:28.827
Toss this on the fire.

00:32:28.861 --> 00:32:30.965
Saffron, skunks,
cabbage, and trillium -

00:32:30.998 --> 00:32:33.570
It'll block our scent and
hers until we're ready.

00:32:33.604 --> 00:32:35.407
Stuff stinks. Well, that's the idea.

00:32:35.441 --> 00:32:37.110
Dust your clothes with the ashes

00:32:37.144 --> 00:32:39.415
And you'll stand a chance
of not being detected.

00:32:39.449 --> 00:32:41.085
You sure they'll come after her?

00:32:41.118 --> 00:32:43.256
Yeah. Vampires mate for life.

00:32:43.289 --> 00:32:45.760
She means more to the
leader than the gun.

00:32:45.793 --> 00:32:47.731
But the blood sickness
is gonna wear off soon,

00:32:47.764 --> 00:32:49.201
So you don't have a lot of time.

00:32:49.234 --> 00:32:50.703
Half-Hour ought to do it.

00:32:50.737 --> 00:32:53.510
And then i want you out of
the area as fast as you can.

00:32:53.544 --> 00:32:54.745
But -

00:32:54.778 --> 00:32:56.348
You can't take care
of them all yourself.

00:32:56.383 --> 00:32:58.719
I'll have her and the colt.

00:32:58.753 --> 00:33:02.260
But after, we're gonna meet up, right?

00:33:02.294 --> 00:33:05.901
Use the gun together, right?

00:33:07.804 --> 00:33:10.176
You're leaving again, aren't you?

00:33:12.347 --> 00:33:15.820
You still want to go
after the demon alone?

00:33:15.853 --> 00:33:17.324
You know, i don't get you.

00:33:17.357 --> 00:33:19.928
You can't treat us like this. Like what?

00:33:19.963 --> 00:33:21.131
Like children.

00:33:21.165 --> 00:33:24.304
You are my children. I'm
trying to keep you safe.

00:33:24.338 --> 00:33:27.143
Dad, all due respect, but
that's a bunch of crap.

00:33:28.079 --> 00:33:30.216
Excuse me?

00:33:30.250 --> 00:33:32.287
You know what sammy
and i have been hunting.

00:33:32.320 --> 00:33:34.592
Hell, you sent us on a
few hunting trips yourself.

00:33:34.626 --> 00:33:36.762
You can't be that worried
about keeping us safe.

00:33:36.795 --> 00:33:38.332
It's not the same thing, de.

00:33:38.366 --> 00:33:39.469
Then what is it?

00:33:39.502 --> 00:33:41.539
Why do you want us out of the big fight?

00:33:41.573 --> 00:33:43.409
This demon...

00:33:43.442 --> 00:33:46.583
It's a bad son of a bitch.

00:33:46.616 --> 00:33:48.152
I can't make the same moves

00:33:48.185 --> 00:33:50.491
If i'm worried about keeping you alive.

00:33:50.524 --> 00:33:51.693
You can't be as reckless.

00:33:51.726 --> 00:33:53.129
Look...

00:33:53.162 --> 00:33:56.736
I don't expect to make it out
of this fight in one piece.

00:33:58.939 --> 00:34:02.380
Your mother's death...

00:34:02.414 --> 00:34:04.017
It almost killed me.

00:34:05.654 --> 00:34:09.529
I can't watch my children die, too.

00:34:09.562 --> 00:34:10.698
I won't.

00:34:10.731 --> 00:34:12.768
What happens if you die?

00:34:12.802 --> 00:34:14.772
Dad, what happens if you die

00:34:14.806 --> 00:34:17.277
And we could have done
something about it?

00:34:17.310 --> 00:34:18.547
You know, i've been thinking.

00:34:18.580 --> 00:34:20.450
I think maybe sammy's
right about this one.

00:34:20.483 --> 00:34:22.120
I think we should do this together.

00:34:24.391 --> 00:34:26.995
We're stronger as a family,
dad. We just are. You know it.

00:34:28.466 --> 00:34:30.069
We're running out of time.

00:34:31.505 --> 00:34:34.177
You do your job, and
you get out of the area.

00:34:35.413 --> 00:34:37.350
That's an order.

00:34:47.337 --> 00:34:49.541
Is there any sign of those three?

00:34:49.574 --> 00:34:51.512
No. Something else.

00:34:51.545 --> 00:34:53.617
What? Luther, they cut off hank's head.

00:34:53.650 --> 00:34:55.721
And kate?

00:34:55.754 --> 00:34:58.760
I don't know. She wasn't there.

00:35:00.229 --> 00:35:01.900
What are we gonna do?

00:35:07.210 --> 00:35:09.782
It's just a truck up on the highway.

00:35:14.892 --> 00:35:17.330
Kate.

00:35:17.363 --> 00:35:19.634
She's in that truck.

00:36:19.889 --> 00:36:21.325
Boo.

00:36:37.523 --> 00:36:39.761
I told you i'd come back.

00:36:58.565 --> 00:37:00.670
Luther: get out!

00:37:04.912 --> 00:37:06.148
Who are you?

00:37:06.180 --> 00:37:07.517
The name's winchester.

00:37:07.550 --> 00:37:08.987
Where are your friends?

00:37:09.020 --> 00:37:10.589
Cleaning out your nest.

00:37:12.928 --> 00:37:14.631
Where's kate?

00:37:14.664 --> 00:37:16.802
Come here, sweetheart.

00:37:24.417 --> 00:37:26.353
Kate, you all right?

00:37:28.257 --> 00:37:30.496
Dead man's blood.

00:37:30.529 --> 00:37:32.567
You son of a bitch.

00:37:32.600 --> 00:37:36.273
I want the colt
- Elkins' gun.

00:37:36.307 --> 00:37:37.309
Trade.

00:37:37.342 --> 00:37:38.712
Is that what this is all about?

00:37:38.746 --> 00:37:40.549
I mean, you can't shoot us all, right?

00:37:40.583 --> 00:37:42.019
We'll kill you.

00:37:42.053 --> 00:37:44.691
Oh, i don't need it for you.

00:37:44.724 --> 00:37:47.697
I'm saving it for something else.

00:37:47.730 --> 00:37:51.303
Now, put the colt
down or she goes first.

00:37:51.337 --> 00:37:53.942
All right.

00:37:53.977 --> 00:37:56.248
Just don't hurt her.

00:38:03.595 --> 00:38:04.864
Back up.

00:38:07.036 --> 00:38:08.404
Further.

00:38:20.328 --> 00:38:22.834
That's a nice move. You almost made it.

00:38:47.482 --> 00:38:48.517
Ugh!

00:38:52.994 --> 00:38:55.498
Don't! I'll break his neck.

00:38:55.531 --> 00:38:57.203
Put the blade down.

00:39:10.495 --> 00:39:13.100
You people.

00:39:13.135 --> 00:39:15.139
Why can't you just leave us alone?

00:39:15.172 --> 00:39:17.475
We have as much right to live as you do.

00:39:17.509 --> 00:39:19.046
John: i don't think so.

00:39:45.665 --> 00:39:48.338
Luther!

00:40:03.502 --> 00:40:05.605
Kate, don't!

00:40:29.520 --> 00:40:31.524
So, boys...

00:40:35.832 --> 00:40:37.503
Yes, sir?

00:40:37.536 --> 00:40:40.074
You ignored a direct order back there.

00:40:40.107 --> 00:40:42.479
Yes, sir. But we saved your ass.

00:40:47.790 --> 00:40:49.192
You're right.

00:40:49.225 --> 00:40:51.531
I am?

00:40:51.564 --> 00:40:53.935
It scares the hell out of me.

00:40:53.968 --> 00:40:55.839
You two are all i've got.

00:40:57.743 --> 00:41:01.484
But i guess we are stronger as a family.

00:41:01.517 --> 00:41:04.189
So...

00:41:04.222 --> 00:41:07.896
We go after this damn thing...

00:41:07.930 --> 00:41:09.866
Together.

00:41:09.900 --> 00:41:12.138
Yes, sir.Yes, sir.

00:00:02.191 --> 00:00:03.694
<font color="#ffff00" size=14>www.tvsubtitles.net</font>
